19. DATACLASS - ADVANCED
------------------------
Dataclass = Shortcut to make Class. No need to write __init__ yourself.

Old - Normal Class - You write __init__:
class BankAccount:
    def __init__(self, name, balance):
        self.name = name
        self.balance = balance
    def show(self):
        return f"{self.name} has {self.balance} rupees"

New - Dataclass - Python writes __init__ for you:
from dataclasses import dataclass

@dataclass
class BankAccount:
    name: str
    balance: float
    def show(self):
        return f"{self.name} has {self.balance} rupees"

a1 = BankAccount("Hyarel", 1000)
print(a1.show())

Output Both:
Hyarel has 1000 rupees

Dataclass Parent + Child - Full:
from dataclasses import dataclass

@dataclass
class BankAccount:
    name: str
    balance: float
    def show(self):
        return f"{self.name} has {self.balance} rupees"

@dataclass
class SavingsAccount(BankAccount):
    interest: float
    def add_interest(self):
        self.balance = self.balance + self.interest
        return f"{self.name} new balance with interest is {self.balance}"
    def show_interest(self):
        return f"{self.name} interest is {self.interest}"

a1 = BankAccount("Hyarel", 1000)
print(a1.show())
s1 = SavingsAccount("Priya", 1000, 100)
print(s1.show())
print(s1.add_interest())
print(s1.show_interest())

Output:
Hyarel has 1000 rupees
Priya has 1000 rupees
Priya new balance with interest is 1100
Priya interest is 100

Important: Rest all same. Only __init__ replaced by @dataclass. In Dataclass Child, no need super().__init__, Python does automatically.
Dataclass = Less code, same work.


