27. NUMPY - ADVANCED
--------------------
Numpy = Fast Maths for Big Numbers. List is good for 10 numbers. Numpy is good for 1 lakh numbers. Fast maths in 1 line.

Old - List - Need loop - Slow:
balances = [1000, 500, 2000]
new_balances = []
for b in balances:
    new_balances.append(b + 100)
print(new_balances)
Output: [1100, 600, 2100]

New - Numpy - No loop - Fast:
import numpy as np
balances = np.array([1000, 500, 2000])
new_balances = balances + 100
print(new_balances)
print(balances.mean())
print(balances.sum())
print(balances.max())

Output:
[1100  600 2100]
1166.66
3500
2000

How it works:
import numpy as np - Take toolbox, np is short name.
np.array([...]) - Make Numpy Array - Like List but fast.
balances + 100 - Adds 100 to all at once - List cannot do this, Numpy can.
mean() - Average, sum() - Total, max() - Biggest.

Why Numpy?
Pandas uses Numpy inside.
Matplotlib uses Numpy inside.
AI / ML needs Numpy - Vectors in ChromaDB are Numpy arrays.

